# Generated datasets — reproducible from a seed, never committed
data/**

# ...except the model's answers, which are the one thing here that is not
# reproducible from a seed. A dataset is a pure function of its seed, so
# committing one is redundant. A completion depends on weights, a quantisation
# and a daemon, none of which live in this repository - so committing these is
# the only way `milan ablate` can produce the published 19.5% on a machine
# with no GPU, no Ollama and no API key. 85K, and it is what turns "here are
# our numbers" into "here are our numbers, and here is the run".
!data/llm-cache/
!data/llm-cache/**
!data/.gitkeep
!data/README.md

